    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ</span></b> , dat. sg. neut. of ὁ, ἡ, τό, used
		abs., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>therefore, in this wise,
				then,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, v.
			ὁ, ἡ, τό, <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> VIII. <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i> a, b; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ οὔτε περισπᾶται οὔτε
				σὺν τῷ ῑ γράφεται</span> (i.e. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τώ</span></b> ) <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				199.2
			</span></i>: written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὼ</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				26.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ;</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνι;</span> dat. sg. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς;</span>
			<i>who?</i> but </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῳ,</span> enclit. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί,</span> dat. sg. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τις</span>, <i>some one.</i></div>
